  "note": "A single open limestone vault spans Shaharah’s narrow rocky gorge. The model follows the mapped footbridge, with a shallow stepped deck, rough parapets, a west gateway, small retaining-wall arches, and stairs along the east cliff. The 2488 m datum is tied to the standard terrain around the crossing. A narrow cutout and a matching faceted relief patch restore the missing under-arch space. Both stair approaches transition to the same standard grid. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
